From 0b0ba4c2b18173303b46dd8ec381735e1615b313 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aa24aa <2496788660@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:05:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(gdn): FP16-accumulate MMA with FP32 carry for the SM12x
 delta-rule prefill kernels

On GeForce Blackwell the FP32-accumulate warp MMA runs at half the rate of the
FP16-accumulate form (RTX 5090, m16n8k16: 254 vs 505 TFLOP/s), and every GEMM of
the SM120 CuTe-DSL GDN prefill kernels uses it (about 88% of the non-CP block
time is the FP32-accumulate MMA floor).

FLASHINFER_GDN_FP16_ACCUM_MMA=1 (private kwarg _fp16_accum_mma of
chunk_gated_delta_rule) now runs the non-CP kernel and the CP T/MN/prefill
stages on FP16-accumulate m16n8k16: 4 K steps accumulate in FP16 and are added
into FP32 accumulators. The state, the output accumulation, the epilogues and
the output/state/checkpoint dtypes stay as they are; the derived MMA operands
(state, V - S K, NewV, QK, T, X, M) are FP16 and bf16 Q/K tiles are converted
to FP16 in shared memory once per block. The mode is off by default and the PTX
of all SM120 kernels is byte-identical with it off.

RTX 5090, CUDA 13.0, benchmarks/bench_gdn_prefill.py (bench_fi), Qwen3.5-27B heads:
  fp16  8x8192  3.027 -> 2.092 ms (1.45x)   1x32768 2.815 -> 2.060 ms (1.37x)
  bf16  8x8192  3.014 -> 2.117 ms (1.42x)   1x32768 2.825 -> 2.112 ms (1.34x)

(cherry picked from commit c0771c79b7e2f2bc0edf4fdcb7c43b986a56707a)
